title: No page says how to see someone else's notes on the first day, though 'docs/README.org' links Jeff's public notes.
pid: 3079757c-5eab-4f2b-a70e-a2444e2ef1a2
body: |2-
  The pieces are on three pages: notes are shared as git repositories
  ('data-model_friendly.org'); another's skgrepo is a config entry
  with 'foreign = true' ('setup.org'); a changed config needs
  'skg-rebuild-session-lifetime-stores' ('setup.org', inside a
  paragraph about two users sharing a data tree). Nothing puts them in
  order, nor names a note of Jeff's to open first. 'docs/README.org'
  links his repository as where the documentation is, not as
  something to read in skg.
  Change: a section "reading Jeff's public notes": clone the
  repository beside your own data, add its three lines to the config,
  rebuild, and go to a root of his whose ID the page gives.
